📚 Subarray & Array-Sum DSA Questions
🟢 Level 1 — Basic Subarray Practice
#	Question	What you have to do
1	Print All Subarrays	Print every possible contiguous subarray.
2	Sum of Every Subarray	Find and print the sum of each possible subarray.
3	Maximum Sum Subarray ⭐	Find the contiguous subarray having the largest sum.
4	Minimum Sum Subarray	Find the contiguous subarray having the smallest sum.
5	Maximum Product Subarray	Find the contiguous subarray whose product is maximum.
6	Minimum Product Subarray	Find the contiguous subarray whose product is minimum.
🟡 Level 2 — Fixed Size Subarrays
#	Question	What you have to do
7	Maximum Sum Subarray of Size K	Find the maximum sum among subarrays containing exactly K elements.
8	Minimum Sum Subarray of Size K	Find the minimum sum among subarrays containing exactly K elements.
9	Maximum Average Subarray of Size K	Find the subarray of exactly K elements having the highest average.
10	Minimum Average Subarray of Size K	Find the subarray of exactly K elements having the lowest average.
11	Print All Subarrays of Size K	Print only contiguous subarrays containing exactly K elements.

Example:

arr = {2, 1, 5, 1, 3, 2}
K = 3

Possible subarrays:

{2,1,5}
{1,5,1}
{5,1,3}
{1,3,2}
🟠 Level 3 — Subarray With Conditions
#	Question	What you have to do
12	Count Subarrays With Sum K	Count how many contiguous subarrays have sum exactly K.
13	Print Subarrays With Sum K	Print all subarrays whose sum is exactly K.
14	Find Subarray With Sum K	Find whether a contiguous subarray with sum K exists.
15	Longest Subarray With Sum K	Find the longest contiguous subarray whose sum is K.
16	Shortest Subarray With Sum K	Find the shortest contiguous subarray whose sum is K.
17	Count Subarrays With Sum Greater Than K	Count subarrays whose sum is greater than K.
18	Count Subarrays With Sum Less Than K	Count subarrays whose sum is less than K.
🔵 Level 4 — Maximum/Minimum Variations
#	Question	What you have to do
19	Print Maximum Sum Subarray	Find the maximum-sum subarray and print its elements.
20	Maximum Sum + Starting/Ending Index	Find maximum sum and the indexes where that subarray starts and ends.
21	Maximum Sum Subarray With At Least K Elements	Find the largest sum where the subarray contains at least K elements.
22	Maximum Sum Subarray With Exactly K Elements	Find the largest sum where the subarray contains exactly K elements.
23	Maximum Sum of Two Non-Overlapping Subarrays	Find two separate subarrays whose combined sum is maximum.
24	Minimum Sum of Two Non-Overlapping Subarrays	Find two separate subarrays whose combined sum is minimum.
